---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

const APP_STORE_URL =
	'https://apps.apple.com/us/app/yardguard-weed-id-removal/id6762166580';
---

<Layout
	title="Projects"
	description="Projects page"
	showDate={false}
	appStoreId="6762166580"
>
	<section class="project">
		<a
			class="project-icon-link"
			href={APP_STORE_URL}
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer"
			aria-label="Download YardGuard on the App Store"
		>
			<img
				src="/images/yardguard-icon.png"
				alt="YardGuard app icon"
				class="project-icon"
				width="120"
				height="120"
				loading="lazy"
			/>
		</a>

		<h2 class="project-title">YardGuard: Weed ID &amp; Removal</h2>

		<p>
			In January of 2025, I bought my first house. This means I am now solely
			responsible for a yard with a flowerbed. Some people's green thumb comes
			natural, some are comfortable "winging" their yard care. I don't fall into
			either category. I got tired of using Google and ChatGPT to ask for
			lawncare advice because the information on both of these platforms can be
			inconsistent and very overwhelming to someone just trying to get started.
			This app makes weed identification and plant care instructions as simple as
			snapping a picture and getting consistent and repeatable advice. The app
			also tells you exactly what lawncare supplies you need and gives you
			convenient Amazon links. I learned a lot throughout this process and plan
			to write a separate piece on the journey at some point.
		</p>

		<p class="project-tagline">
			Don't let lawncare overwhelm you. Try YardGuard today!
		</p>

		<a
			class="project-cta"
			href={APP_STORE_URL}
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer"
		>
			Download on the App Store
		</a>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.project {
		text-align: center;
	}
	.project-icon-link {
		display: inline-block;
		border: none;
	}
	.project-icon {
		width: 120px;
		height: 120px;
		border-radius: 22%;
		box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
		transition: transform 0.15s ease;
	}
	.project-icon-link:hover .project-icon {
		transform: scale(1.03);
	}
	.project-title {
		margin: 0.75em 0 0.5em;
	}
	.project p {
		text-align: left;
	}
	.project-tagline {
		text-align: center !important;
		font-style: italic;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
	}
	.project-cta {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-top: 0.5em;
		padding: 0.6em 1.2em;
		border-radius: 8px;
		background: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
		color: rgb(var(--gray-light));
		text-decoration: none;
		font-weight: 500;
	}
	.project-cta:hover {
		text-decoration: none;
		opacity: 0.9;
	}
</style>
